# Dine In UI Asset Convention

- Before creating or changing UI, search the project for existing 9-slice frames, buttons, icons, fonts, and prefabs.
- Reuse those authored assets instead of drawing plain replacement rectangles or introducing a new visual style.
- Keep new UI editable through prefabs and serialized Inspector fields for layout, colors, assets, timing, and audio routing.
- Use the established Dine In colors and Fredoka typography unless a feature already has a more specific authored style.
- Keep UI polish separate from authoritative gameplay logic and avoid duplicate presentation systems.
- Verify both direct scene play and normal build flow after UI changes.
